Verified behavior:
- UniversalTuningDimension distinguishes System vs Workload scope and requires explicit Id, AuthorityId and candidate values.
- UniversalTuningSearchSpacePlanner builds a deterministic bounded Cartesian product only from explicitly declared values.
- blank identity/authority/value, duplicate dimension id and duplicate candidate value fail closed.
- zero dimensions produce zero candidates; no empty/default tuning candidate is invented.
- MaxCandidates truncates a deterministic prefix; no randomization or hidden exploration axis is introduced.
- universal search-space candidates carry no evidence, confidence or recommendation authority.
- UniversalTuningSystemDimensionFactory projects only an already-authorized WindowsCapabilityCandidatePlan with CanExplore=true.
- Unavailable, MissingCurrentState, NoCandidateSpace, or Ready-with-zero-candidates remain absent from universal tuning space.
- Windows target values are preserved exactly in ExplorationRank order; duplicate target values fail closed.
- the bridge does not read the registry, generate new schema points, mutate Windows, consult recommendations, or publish recommendation authority.
- existing BlueStacks/FF TuningCandidate and Auto Tuner paths remain source-compatible and unchanged.
- no startup discovery or tuning side effect was added.

Authority invariant:
Support/search space is exploration only. It never means recommended, validated, or safe-to-persist. Existing typed evidence, repeatability, freshness/fingerprint, Global Controlled Benchmark Lease, validation challenge and winner-promotion gates remain authoritative.

